TITLE:: RCSession
summary:: The rig: server, clock, OSC port, MIDI and the registry of songs
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Guides/reCurrent, Classes/RCSong

DESCRIPTION::
One session per sclang process. Nothing is created at class-load time: a piece bootstrap calls link::#*boot::, which is idempotent (a running clock is never re-created, an already open port is fine, MIDI is initialised once). The library never stops the clock.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: boot
Create or update the default session.
argument:: server
Defaults to code::Server.default::.
argument:: clock
A clock to use. When nil, a permanent code::LinkClock:: is created unless a running clock exists.
argument:: oscPort
UDP port to open for OSC control (nil: none).
argument:: initMidi
When true, code::MIDIClient.init:: and code::MIDIIn.connectAll:: once.
returns:: the session

METHOD:: default
The current session, or nil before boot.

METHOD:: killAll
Stop every beat of every song. Frees nothing else (emergency handle).

METHOD:: reset
Free all songs and forget the session (tests).

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: server
METHOD:: clock
METHOD:: localAddr
The code::NetAddr:: OSC defs listen to (127.0.0.1, any port).
METHOD:: songs
code::IdentityDictionary:: name → link::Classes/RCSong::.
METHOD:: song
argument:: name
METHOD:: killAll
METHOD:: free

EXAMPLES::

code::
RCSession.boot(s, oscPort: 32345);
RCSession.boot(Server.default, TempoClock.new(2).permanent_(true), oscPort: nil, initMidi: false);   // tests, no hardware
::
